---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import Status from '../../components/Status.astro';
import Film from '../../components/Film.astro';
import { url } from '../../data/url';
---
<Base slug="decisions/" title="Open decisions and glossary" description="The decisions still open for The Cousin, and the words used across these pages.">
  <header class="wrap phead">
    <p class="chapter">13 · Decisions</p>
    <h1 class="h1" data-split="lines" data-intro>What we still need to decide together.</h1>
    <div class="headrow" data-reveal="up" data-intro data-delay="0.3">
      <p class="lede muted">These are the calls for the founders, taken from the handoff and the v2 plan. Where a recommendation exists, it is shown; none is settled.</p>
      <Status s="open" />
    </div>
  </header>
  <section class="wrap row">
    <p class="chapter">Design decisions</p>
    <div class="tbl" tabindex="0"><table><thead><tr><th>Decision</th><th>Recommendation so far</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Should the AI choose the final picks from the safe shortlist?</td><td>Yes, after a one-day test</td></tr><tr><td>How wide is the first product?</td><td>A narrow first slice; design the data model for sessions and offers now</td></tr><tr><td>Does the card-and-edit model feel right?</td><td>Assumed yes; never explicitly confirmed</td></tr><tr><td>After “scrap it”, do today’s facts carry over, said aloud?</td><td>Assumed yes</td></tr><tr><td>A swipeable ideas screen?</td><td>Part of the proposed clean-sheet design</td></tr><tr><td>Paid placement, if ever</td><td>No policy yet</td></tr><tr><td>Step 0: be the cousin by hand for two weeks with a spreadsheet, to prove friends actually go</td><td>Recommended, never confirmed</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
  </section>
  <section class="wrap row">
    <p class="chapter">Build decisions (v2 plan)</p>
    <div class="tbl" tabindex="0"><table><thead><tr><th>Decision</th><th>Recommendation so far</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Accept the inverted build order: critics and listening first?</td><td>Yes</td></tr><tr><td>A bounded agent for the hardest requests in the first version?</td><td>After the simpler routes are stable</td></tr><tr><td>Agree the ten stress-test gates, or change the targets</td><td>Open</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
  </section>
  <section class="wrap row">
    <p class="chapter">Still open from the brief</p>
    <div class="prose"><p>Business model. Target group beyond friends. Privacy details: what is stored, for how long, export and deletion. Monthly API budget. Team and hours per week. A data source for events and showtimes.</p></div>
  </section>
  <section class="wrap row">
    <p class="chapter">Already decided</p>
    <div class="tbl" tabindex="0"><table><thead><tr><th>Topic</th><th>Decision</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Surface</td><td>Our own app; no WhatsApp or Telegram</td></tr><tr><td>Language</td><td>English first</td></tr><tr><td>End goal</td><td>Voice in, voice out, plan pinned on a live map (later)</td></tr><tr><td>Scope now</td><td>One city, one evening; intercity and multi-day parked</td></tr><tr><td>Bookings and payments</td><td>Later; always need the person’s explicit yes</td></tr><tr><td>Visited places</td><td>Rest before coming back; clubs are the exception</td></tr><tr><td>Taste change</td><td>Listening plus a monthly catch-up; the meter only brings the catch-up forward</td></tr><tr><td>ML</td><td>Fences, facts and the route solver are never learned; a model replaces a rule only after winning a live test</td></tr><tr><td>Diet, allergy, access</td><td>Count only when the place itself confirmed them</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
  </section>
  <section class="wrap row">
    <p class="chapter">Glossary</p>
    <div class="tbl" tabindex="0"><table><thead><tr><th>Word</th><th>Meaning</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Fence</td><td>A rule that must be true, yes or no</td></tr><tr><td>Magnet</td><td>Something they’d like; it ranks, never rules out</td></tr><tr><td>Notebook</td><td>What the cousin knows about one person</td></tr><tr><td>Card</td><td>The summary of one conversation: who, what, rules, tastes</td></tr><tr><td>Safe / stretch / wild</td><td>The three kinds of idea in a list</td></tr><tr><td>Rest period</td><td>A fading penalty after a visit</td></tr><tr><td>Pin</td><td>A place asked for by name; beats the rest period</td></tr><tr><td>Arc</td><td>The shape of an evening: easy start, main thing, gentle end</td></tr><tr><td>Verdict</td><td>Serve, substitute, ask, can’t, won’t or not ours</td></tr><tr><td>Bandit</td><td>A method that learns by trying (Thompson sampling)</td></tr><tr><td>Embedding</td><td>Numbers that capture what a place feels like</td></tr><tr><td>Live test</td><td>Half see A, half see B; compare what happened</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
  </section>
</Base>
